WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.669
-Hasan, here's how
we're going to do this.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:07.306
You and I will each take turns
telling a story to our audience

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.642
about one topic. Okay?
-Okay.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.179
-Tonight's topic is...
[ Drum roll ]

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.814
...embarrassing parents.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.550
-All right. Okay.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.786
-Since you're my guest,
I'm going to give you the honor

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.155
of watching me go first.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.456
You can take your place
over there by the --

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.624
-Okay.
-I'll start off.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.992
Okay, here we go.
-All right, go ahead.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.795
-All right. I have so many
embarrassing parent stories.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.931
I'm trying to think.
I don't know which one to --

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.700
-You picked the topic
because I'm Indian, right?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.034
-No, I didn't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:36.436
-Yeah, you did.
-No, it was at random.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.005
No, I promise, no.
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:41.407
-Please, I'm Irish.
I got some bad ones, too.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:45.744
Yeah. What do we got?
I mean, my mom's got so many.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.648
I'll do -- I'll do my dad
because I talked to him today.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.182
So he reminded me of this story.

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:54.053
My dad was very -- We never had
any luck with cars growing up.

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:56.256
We just never had a great car.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:59.058
And I remember we finally
did get a nice car.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.793
It was a Cutlass Ciera.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.528
That was the name of it.
It even sounds fancy.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.464
And I think it had, like,
cloth seats,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.664
which was a big deal for us.

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:07.133
'Cause the seats would be vinyl

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.567
and just be too hot
and everything.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.670
Like, we just burn --
we'd burn our flesh and stuff.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.738
[ Laughter ]
But, no, this was like,

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.307
"Wow, luxury."
And it was amazing.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.076
And so one night,
he was coming home from work.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.312
And we used to wait out for
the car and stuff like that

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:22.148
when my dad would come --
Me and my sister and my mom.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.983
So the car was coming down the
street and the horn was honking.

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:27.253
[ Imitates horn honking ]

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.488
And my mom was like,
"oh, my God, kids, come out.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:31.157
Let's greet --
Let's say hi to daddy outside.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.226
I think he won the lottery.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.561
I think we won the lottery."

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.529
And we're like
"Oh, my gosh. What?"

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:39.098
And, like, she was almost
crying.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.334
We ran out to the driveway
and the car is honking.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.801
Beep! Beep! Beep! Beep!

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.470
And my dad gets out
and slams the door,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.972
and the car is still honking.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.741
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.711
"The horn's broke."
Didn't even look at us.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.246
Just walked right past us
and got a beer.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.381
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.618
And then another thing happened
to my dad's car.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:02.021
He was --
He was trying to fix his car.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.690
And he got a thing called,
like, Gunk-Out or something

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.858
that you spray on the engine.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:07.460
My dad does not know anything
about cars.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.863
He's from Brooklyn, New York.
Barely knows how to drive a car.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.498
But he's fixing his car
in the driveway.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.800
And he's spraying this thing.
And he turns on the engine on.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.902
And the car lights on fire.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:19.239
So my dad's freaking out.
He doesn't know what to do.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.908
So he slams the hood closed.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.011
And it's like flames
growing out the sides.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.979
And he's like,
"Oh, maybe that was a mistake.

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:28.514
Maybe I should try
to open it up again

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:29.716
to get the flames to go out.
-Oh, no.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.384
-So he went
and he popped the hood.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.252
And then went around.
It had one of those, like,

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.388
kind of locks in the front
that it's really hard to open.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.490
So he was burning his fingers.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.992
And he couldn't open the hood.
And he just came in.

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.761
He goes, "Kids,
just get on the ground.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.730
I think the car
is going to blow up."

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.897
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.265
And we laid on the ground.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.968
And my mom's, like,
"We got to tell the neighbors."

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.269
'Cause they had their kids.
He was like --

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.571
And he yelled over to them.
He's like, "Go inside.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.873
My car is about to explode."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:56.742
And the kids ran in.
And people were screaming.

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:59.145
And we called
the fire department.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.379
And we were laying
on the ground.

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:01.847
And then they came --
-But, you guys stayed?

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:03.616
-Oh, we stayed and just
laid on the ground.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.750
Like -- just hoping.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:05.918
-They ran for it.
Let them be safe.

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:07.353
-Oh, yeah. Our neighbors
ran down the street.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.788
Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:11.124
And they put out the thing.
And my dad's car was totaled.

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.860
He burnt --
Every wire was stripped.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.161
And there was nothing on it.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.263
And that was the last time
we ever got a nice car.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.397
There you go. That's my story.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.199
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.101
♪♪

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.936
-I got to go now?
-Yeah, now it's your turn.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:25.905
Okay.
-All right.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.307
Now send it up.
-All right. So this like --

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.708
this is a competition?
This is, like, a --

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.143
-Oh, maybe.
-Is it?

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.378
-No I think it's more of a fun
story telling thing. But --

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.512
-No, no, no. I just not --

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:34.880
I don't want participation
points.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.949
I want to win or lose it.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.016
-Okay, all right,
all right, all right.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.117
[ Laughter ]
Go for it.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.886
-I got to -- Okay, okay.
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.620
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.789
-Okay, I -- [ Laughs ]

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.692
Okay. I have -- I'm okay.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.959
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.660
No, I have to think about
what are the repercussions

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.762
if I tell this,
but who cares?

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.963
Let's just -- let's do this.
All right.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:53.833
[ Laughter ]
So -- because I got to win.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.302
So when I was in high school,

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.470
I told a lot of stories
about growing up.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.671
But -- I don't know
if you guys know this,

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.074
but I wasn't very good
at math or science.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.377
I'm sorry.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.346
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:08.581
I know.
I've let our people down. But...

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.649
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:14.219
So I was failing Honors Chem.

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.689
And, so sometimes during lunch,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:20.759
I would have lunch
in Mr. Delucas' classroom.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.129
You know,
like all popular kids do.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.664
[ Laughter ]
And hang out.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.332
Hang out with the teacher
during lunch.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.201
-Eating --
-So I'm in there during lunch.

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:30.970
Mr. Delucas is like, "Hey,
I got to go to the bathroom.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.606
Just give me a minute
I'll be right back."

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.442
He leaves to go to the bathroom.
I look at his desk.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.845
And the homework solutions
manual

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:41.914
is just sitting
right there on the desk.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:45.718
And it's just looking at me
like the Sports Almanac

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.321
in "Back to the Future."
Like, "I have all the answers.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:51.824
[ Laughter ]
Just pick me up."

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:55.361
And I was like, "He'll never
guess that if I take this --

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:58.163
he won't even know it was me.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:00.399
He's not going to guess that
the Indian kid did it.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.568
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:05.304
So I take the solutions manual.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.273
I put it in my backpack.
I walk out of the class.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:09.575
And I'm like,
"Okay, this is wrong.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.277
What you are doing
is objectively wrong."

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.812
And I know -- like,
I feel awful about it.

00:05:13.812 --> 00:05:15.714
I have kids.
I should not do this.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.316
Cheating is wrong. But...

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.218
I've never felt more alive.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.686
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:22.021
And I'm like,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:25.324
"What if I go to Kinko's

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:29.361
and I just photocopy this,
and I sell it to other kids?"

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:31.564
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, gosh.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.167
-And so I'm at Kinko's,
and I just photocopy the book.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:37.469
I come back to school.
And I just start selling

00:05:37.469 --> 00:05:39.605
the answer to the homework
to other kids

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.307
for $5 a pop,
which is a discount.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.542
That's a discount.
It's a great deal!

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.809
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:45.511
All the answers for
the entire year, five bucks?

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.814
And, eventually,
someone snitched.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:51.016
I don't know who it was.
It was Michael Minichiello.

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:53.753
But I don't know who it was.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.655
And I don't know. I just --
I don't know who it could be.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.659
And Mr. Delucas calls me
into his classroom.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.227
And he sits me down.
And is like,

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:05.831
"I know you're the kid
who stole the solutions manual.

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.500
And, Hasan,
what you have done --

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.802
you have violated my trust,

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:13.806
you've insulted the ethical
standards of this school,

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.675
And I should expel you
right now.

00:06:16.675 --> 00:06:18.544
But I'm going to call
your father instead."

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.112
And I was like,
"Just expel me, please."

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:23.615
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:26.185
He puts my dad on speakerphone.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:29.955
"Mr. Minhaj, come to
Davis High School immediately.

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:32.391
I am waiting here
with your son."

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:33.692
It was the longest 45 minutes

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:35.061
I've ever had to go through
in my life.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.997
I'm sitting there. There's just
an empty chair, sweating.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.232
I'm like, "I'm going to die."

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:41.667
My dad comes in. He sits down.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:46.105
Mr. Delucas is like, "Your son
is the criminal master mind

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:48.840
behind one of
the biggest cheating scandals

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.442
at this school.

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:54.480
He has been selling
the homework answers

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.116
to multiple students
in his class."

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.984
And my dad,
he looks at Mr. Delucas.

00:06:58.984 --> 00:07:01.553
and he was like, "Mr. Delucas,

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:04.757
my son did not do this."

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.425
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:10.996
And I was like, "Wow.
Like, pops, like, he trusts me.

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:12.865
[ Laughter ]
He has my back."

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.400
-Wow.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.836
And he's like,
"Hasan is a coward.

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:20.873
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:23.442
He doesn't have the guts
to pull this off."

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:27.212
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.212 --> 00:07:30.282
And I did graduate.

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:31.551
And here I am. So --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:33.285
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you, guys.

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:33.985
♪♪

00:07:33.985 --> 00:07:35.988
-Coward?
-A coward.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:39.358
-Tough dad! That's hilarious.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.327
That is how you do it
right there, everybody.

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.896
Hasan Minhaj!
[ Cheers and applause ]

